#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:0
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:8
msgid "mount-control interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"The `mount-control` interface allows the mounting and unmounting of both "
"transient (non-persistent) and persistent filesystem mount points. The "
"interface does not itself create or maintain mount points, but instead "
"permits the snapped application or service to create and maintain its own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:12
msgid "This interface gives privileged access to the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:14
msgid ""
"To mount a local filesystem, `mount-control` must be used together with the "
"{ref}`block-devices interface <interfaces-block-devices-interface>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:16
msgid "Requires snapd version *2.54+*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:18
msgid "Use of `nfs` requires snapd version *2.67+*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:20
msgid "Use of `cifs` requires snapd version *2.68+*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:22
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Interface management <how-to-guides-work-with-snaps-connect-"
"interfaces>` and {ref}`Supported interfaces <ref-index_interfaces>` for "
"further details on how interfaces are used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:24
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:26
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**: "
"no</br> **{ref}`Super-privileged <reference-operations-interfaces-super-"
"privileged-interfaces>`**: yes</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:26
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:34
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:36
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:38
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:40
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:42
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:30
msgid ""
"This interface controls a resource shared by the whole system. Snaps that "
"use it can be installed as parallel instances, but every instance acts on "
"the same system resource and snapd does not coordinate between them. Make "
"sure each instance manages different resources, or run only one instance at "
"a time. See {ref}`Snaps that are unsupported as parallel instances "
"<interfaces-parallel-installs-shared-resources>` for details.."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:33
msgid "**Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:34
msgid ""
"`persistent` (plug): defines whether the mount can be persistent or not.</"
"br> Either `true` or `false`. Defaults to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:36
msgid ""
"`type` (plug): lists one or more acceptable filesystems for this mount.</"
"br>  Example: `[ext2, ext3, ext4]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:38
msgid ""
"`what` (plug): absolute path of what to mount using a matching wildcard.</"
"br> Example: `/dev/sd*`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:40
msgid ""
"`where` (plug): either an absolute destination path for the mount, or a "
"starting reference to  `$SNAP_COMMON` or `$SNAP_DATA` optionally followed by "
"a path. Wildcards are also supported.</br> Example: `/media/$USER/**`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:42
msgid ""
"`options` (plug, required): a list of one or more permitted options.</br> "
"Example: `[rw, sync]`</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:44
msgid ""
"`namespace` (plug): either `snap`, for locations within the snap, `host`, "
"for locations outside the snap,  or `auto` to set the namespace according to "
"the _where_ pattern. Defaults to `auto`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:46
msgid ""
"See [AppArmor globbing syntax](https://gitlab.com/apparmor/apparmor/-/wikis/"
"AppArmor_Core_Policy_Reference#apparmor-globbing-syntax) for details on how "
"the pattern matching and wildcards work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:48
msgid ""
"It's the responsibility of the snapped application or service to create and "
"maintain a mount point, using either of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:49
msgid "the [mount](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man8/mount.8.html) command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:50
msgid ""
"the [mount()](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/mount.2.html) system call"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:51
msgid ""
"an accompanying {ref}`snapctl mount <how-to-guides-manage-snaps-use-snapctl>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:53
msgid ""
"The `snapctl mount` command is the only option for creating a persistent "
"mount point via its `--persistent` mount option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:55
msgid "Accepted filesystems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:57
msgid ""
"Most filesystem types which are supported by the host system are allowed by "
"this interface, with a few exceptions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:59
msgid "The following filesystems are **not** accepted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:61
msgid ""
"`bpf`, `cgroup`, `cgroup2`, `debugfs`, `devpts`, `encryptfs`, `hugetlbfs`, "
"`overlayfs`, `proc`, `securityfs`, `sysfs`, and `tracefs`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:63
msgid ""
"While other filesystems are accepted, the following filesystems are "
"supported along with their respective filesystem-specific mount options "
"(more on mount options below):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:65
msgid ""
"`adfs`, `affs`, `aufs`, `autofs`, `btrfs`, `cifs`, `ext2`, `ext3`, `ext4`, "
"`fat`, `functionfs`, `fuse`, `hfs`, `hpfs`, `iso9660`, `jfs`, `msdos`, "
"`nfs`, `nfs4`, `ntfs`, `ntfs-3g`, `lowntfs-3g`, `ramfs`, `reiserfs`, "
"`squashfs`, `tmpfs`, `ubifs`, `udf`,` ufs`, `umsdos`, `usbfs`, `vfat`, "
"`xfs`, and `zfs`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:67
msgid ""
"**Note:** If only `tmpfs` is specified, `what` must be `none`. The `tmpfs` "
"type cannot be listed with any other types in a single mount entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:69
msgid ""
"**Note:** When using `nfs` or `cifs` types, attribute `what` must be left "
"out from the mount entry in plug attributes. Since neither of those types "
"can be listed with any other fs types in a the same entry it is recommended "
"do add a separate entry for NFS or CIFS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:71
msgid "Permitted mount options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:73
msgid "The following filesystem-independent mount options are permitted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:75
msgid ""
"`async`, `atime`, `auto`, `bind`, `defaults`, `diratime`, `dirsync`, "
"`iversion`, `lazytime`, `noatime`, `noauto`, `nodev`,  `nodiratime`, "
"`noexec`, `nofail`, `nogroup`, `noiversion`, `nolazytime`, `nomand`, "
"`noowner`, `norelatime`, `nosuid`, `nostrictatime`, `nouser`, `nousers`, "
"`relatime`, `ro`, `rw`, `strictatime`, and `sync`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:77
msgid ""
"**Note:** Option `bind` is only allowed when no filesystem is specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:79
msgid ""
"Filesystem-specific mount options are also permitted, so long as each is "
"supported by every filesystem listed in the corresponding `type` section.  "
"The mount options supported by a given filesystem can usually be found in "
"its respective manpage or in the [mount](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/"
"man8/mount.8.html) manpage.  The complete list of supported filesystem-"
"specific mount options for each filesystem type is included in the [source "
"code](https://github.com/canonical/snapd/blob/master/interfaces/builtin/"
"mount_control.go) for this interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:81
msgid "Code examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/mount-control-interface.md:83
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
" mntctl:\n"
"  interface: mount-control\n"
"  mount:\n"
"  - what: /dev/sd*\n"
"    where: /media/**\n"
"    type: [ext2, ext3, ext4]\n"
"    options: [rw, sync, user_xattr]\n"
"  - what: /usr/**\n"
"    where: $SNAP_COMMON/**\n"
"    options: [bind]\n"
"  - what: /dev/sda{0,1}\n"
"    where: $SNAP_COMMON/**\n"
"    options: [ro]\n"
"  - what: /dev/sdb[0-1]\n"
"    where: $SNAP_COMMON/{foo,other,**}\n"
"    options: [sync]\n"
"  - where: /media/**\n"
"    type: [nfs]\n"
"    options: [rw]\n"
"  - where: /media/**\n"
"    type: [cifs]\n"
"    options: [rw]\n"
"apps:\n"
" app:\n"
"  plugs: [mntctl]\n"
msgstr ""

